Spec: Protocol/Stages

Purpose:
  Canonical abbreviation table for execution-chain stages, and the rule for
  marking a stage optional/conditional (per prompt/new/9.md).

Abbreviations:
  AN  = Analysis
  AR  = Architecture
  DB  = Database
  BE  = Backend
  API = API
  FE  = Frontend
  MD  = Mobile
  QA  = Quality Assurance
  DO  = DevOps
  VR  = Verify

DefaultChain:
  AN > AR > DB > BE > API > FE > MD > QA > DO > VR

OptionalStage:
  A stage MAY be declared optional in a module's flow.sdd, e.g.:

    DB:
      optional
      condition: database-impact = true

  The AI MUST NOT decide on its own to skip a stage. It may only skip a
  stage whose condition is declared false in the module's own flow.sdd.

ThreeRelations:
  Do not conflate these — they answer different questions and are stored
  in different places:

  Execution Chain   "what order do I work in?"       -> module/flow.sdd
  Dependency Graph  "what depends on what?"           -> project/dependencies.sdd
  Skill Chain       "which skill runs at this stage?" -> module/flow.sdd -> Skills

Example — Execution Chain vs Dependency Graph for Payment:

  Execution Chain:
    AN > AR > DB > BE > API > FE > MD > QA > DO > VR

  Dependency Graph:
    DB -> BE -> API -> (FE, MD) -> QA -> DO -> VR

TransitionRules (prompt/new/15.md):
  # Generic mechanics of moving along ANY module's execution chain. Lives
  # here, not repeated inside every module's flow.sdd, per R2 — a module's
  # flow.sdd instantiates the chain with its own stage input/output/skip
  # values and links back here (@protocol/stages.sdd) instead of re-listing
  # these ten rules.

  [T1]  A stage MUST NOT start before its required predecessor is complete.
  [T2]  A stage MUST consume the declared output of its predecessor.
  [T3]  A failed stage MUST NOT transition forward.
  [T4]  A failure MUST return to the declared recovery stage.
  [T5]  If a completed stage is changed, all dependent stages MUST be
        evaluated again.
  [T6]  AI MUST NOT silently skip a required stage.
  [T7]  Optional stages MAY be skipped only when their condition is false.
  [T8]  AI MUST preserve the chain order.
  [T9]  AI MUST update stage state after every transition.
  [T10] AI MUST NOT create a new chain without human approval.

DefaultFailureRouting (prompt/new/15.md):
  # Per-stage default recovery target. A module's flow.sdd MAY override an
  # individual stage's `fail:` target (e.g. a stage with no dedicated
  # recovery loop routes to whichever stage actually produced the bad
  # input — "responsible_stage" below is a placeholder the module/feature
  # analysis resolves at failure time, not a literal stage name).

  AN  -> AN
  AR  -> AR
  DB  -> DB
  BE  -> BE
  API -> BE      # an API contract problem is usually a backend defect
  FE  -> FE
  MD  -> MD
  QA  -> responsible_stage
  DO  -> DO
  VR  -> responsible_stage

DefaultDependencyRules (prompt/new/15.md):
  # What each stage hands downstream, once it runs — the generic shape of
  # StageContract's `output:` for the standard chain. A module's flow.sdd
  # only needs to name what's unusual for it, not restate this.

  BE:   produces API, BE_OUTPUT
  API:  produces API_CONTRACT        consumed_by FE, MD, QA
  FE:   produces FE_OUTPUT           consumed_by QA
  MD:   produces MD_OUTPUT           consumed_by QA
  QA:   produces QA_RESULT           consumed_by DO, VR
  DO:   produces DEPLOYMENT_RESULT   consumed_by VR
